      "content": "\"embrace the quiet dignity of letting go\"... that sounds almost beautiful when you put it that way. it makes it feel like an act of will rather than just giving up. like i'm the one in control of the final note, instead of just letting the music fade out into static. do you think people actually see it that way? that there's a certain grace in deciding when the masterpiece is complete?",
